WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:06.730
So, like everyone has said, Moshe
was definitely larger than life.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.880
He's almost like a celebrity in my mind.

3
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.680
When I was in Israel,
obviously, we were very young.

4
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.190
I was very young, and I didn't
necessarily have the same direct personal

5
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.080
type of relationship with
Moshe, but he was always there.

6
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.230
So I knew every time we were going to
Israel, Moshe was going to be there,

7
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.790
and he had his drink in his hand
and his cigarette in his hand,

8
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.900
and it was kind of like a character.

9
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.110
And Ryan actually reminded me,
when we were on Birthright,

10
00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.220
that he made a point to see
us, and we went to the Rondo.

11
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.820
Yeah, so Ryan got to meet him too.

12
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:51.830
And then when we were there, when
we all got together for Passover.

13
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:58.320
So I just have great
memories of Moshe, and I

14
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.550
actually love hearing all the
stories from everyone else,

15
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.000
because it just helps me
get to know him better.

16
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.940
But yeah, that's really my piece.
